# `fire.py build`'s C++20-coroutine companion unit, beside the `*.ci` and
# `*.o` above: `fire.py` writes `<stem>_gen.cpp` into the CURRENT WORKING
# DIRECTORY, so a build run from the repository root leaves one here and
# nothing reads it. Two of them were committed by e98ea1f8 before this line
# existed. `bugs/TEST_py314_sweep_still_leaves_a_generated_cpp_at_the_repo_root.md`
# has the measurement; the ignore is the cheap half of the fix and the CWD
# itself is the other.
*_gen.cpp
# A hand-written probe left at the repo root under a `tempfile`-shaped name.
# `.mojo` scratch belongs in `.tmp/` (ignored below), but `mkstemp`/a probe run
# from the root puts `tmpXXXXXXXX.mojo` there, and a `git add -A` then tracks
# it. That is not a cosmetic mess: `tools/suite.py::tracked_mojo_files()` feeds
# EVERY tracked top-level `*.mojo` to the bootstrap fanouts, so each leftover
# becomes a bootstrap job that can only fail or, worse, silently widen the
# corpus (the `fcntl` probes `tmphemc8yln.mojo` and `tmpe7tqx39y.mojo` were
# committed this way by 3d32c0e66, and the former turned the gate red at
# c0182fd365). Root-anchored, so a real fixture named `tmp*.mojo` in a
# subdirectory is unaffected.
/tmp*.mojo
mojoc
